@page "/architecture"

<PageTitle>Architecture — IntentBlazor</PageTitle>
<p class="eyebrow">DESIGN FOUNDATION</p>
<h1>Two components.<br />One shared workspace.</h1>
<p class="lead">The developer exposes capabilities. The AI proposes a presentation.
    The runtime validates it and connects the interface to real data and actions.</p>
<div class="card-grid">
    <article class="card"><h2>Core contracts</h2><p>Versioned output documents describe data references,
        state, view nodes, bindings, and interactions.</p></article>
    <article class="card"><h2>Execution runtime</h2><p>Scoped in-memory sessions coordinate validated documents,
        selections, typed sorting, draft edits, and revision checks. Model and application tool execution are planned.</p></article>
    <article class="card"><h2>Blazor presentation</h2><p>The output renderer combines familiar controls and specialist
        surfaces while preserving selections and unfinished edits. Try the authored examples in the playground.</p></article>
</div>
<section>
    <h2>Application authority stays with the developer</h2>
    <p>Generated content cannot grant access or invent a successful save. Application services enforce permissions,
        validation, concurrency, and persistence. Direct selections and edits remain responsive without model calls.</p>
    <p><a href="https://github.com/Kita72/IntentBlazor/tree/main/docs/architecture">Read the architecture decisions on GitHub</a>.</p>
    <p><a href="/playground">Inspect documents, state, and interactions in the playground</a>.</p>
</section>
